                <pb facs="0968" n="840" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg840"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 643.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wallace to Mr.
                            Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-02-24"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 24, 1885</date>.
                        (Received March 9.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 477.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the affair
                    of the American College at Harpoot hastens to a satisfactory settlement. A note
                    from Mr. Barnum, of that institution, informs me that the application for
                    official recognition of the schools has been sent to this city, presumably for
                    ministerial approval.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>LEWIS WALLACE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
